bo, who lived at the end of the first century B.C./early first century A.D., would appear to suggest a figure of approximately 500,000-600,000."<br>Ptolemaic Egypt had three big cities. The largest one is Alexandria on which the data above applies. The numbers for both Memphis and Ptolemais is between 50-100K.<br>In 60 BCE Polybius said Alexandria was the most populous city in the world. His estimate was 300K "free population". Recent estimates put the population near 1 million people  and 300K in 200 BCE . The figure of 300K does not include slaves.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1018, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 939})
