t the only one. According to Shelach and Jaffe (2014) "The inner walls of Zhengzhou enclosed an area of about 300 ha, but the area inside the recently discovered outer walls was as large as 1,500 ha (Fig. 8)." This would provide an estimate of between 60,000-120,000 for the area inside the inner wall.<br>If the city of Zhengzhou is considered to be the whole site, spread over 25km2 or 2500 hectares, the estimated number of inhabitants balloons to 500,000 at the (relatively low) density per hectare of 200 people.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 998, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 951})
